{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01BEU7QP1GmN3NeYcS4sd4WU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good! The syntax is valid. Let me review the logic in my implementation to ensure it will work:\n\nLooking at my `_split_on_death_evidence` implementation:\n\n**Logic Flow:**\n1. For each character with aliases\n2. Collect all mention contexts\n3. Search for death patterns (like \"fell prostrate in death the [NAME]\")\n4. Check if both the canonical name AND an alias appear near death evidence\n5. If yes, split into two characters: one with canonical name, one with aliases\n\n**Potential Issue I Notice:**\nThe death scene in Masque has \"fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\" AND \"seizing the mummer\" in the same context. My code looks for both names near a death pattern, but the logic on line 388-393 might be too strict.\n\nLet me refine the logic to be more robust:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":323,"cache_read_input_tokens":68514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":323,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"076185ae-b8e4-4f9d-b6d1-b2359811f632","uuid":"22a2cfac-7a2d-4f83-ba02-22b35e2e4474"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01BEU7QP1GmN3NeYcS4sd4WU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GeGZFEP279rHhhKZKkc88A","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/src/agents/characters.py","old_string":"            # Check for death evidence involving any pair of names\n            death_evidence = []\n            for i, name1 in enumerate(all_names):\n                for name2 in all_names[i+1:]:\n                    # Check if both names appear in contexts with death language\n                    name1_lower = name1.lower()\n                    name2_lower = name2.lower()\n\n                    # Look for death patterns near these names\n                    for pattern in DEATH_PATTERNS:\n                        matches = list(re.finditer(pattern, combined_context, re.IGNORECASE))\n                        for match in matches:\n                            matched_name = match.group(1).lower()\n                            # If the death pattern mentions one of our names\n                            if matched_name in name1_lower or matched_name in name2_lower:\n                                # And both names appear in nearby context\n                                match_pos = match.start()\n                                context_window = combined_context[max(0, match_pos-200):match_pos+200].lower()\n                                if name1_lower in context_window and name2_lower in context_window:\n                                    death_evidence.append((name1, name2, context_window))","new_string":"            # Check for death evidence involving any pair of names\n            death_evidence = []\n            for i, name1 in enumerate(all_names):\n                for name2 in all_names[i+1:]:\n                    # Check if both names appear in contexts with death language\n                    name1_lower = name1.lower()\n                    name2_lower = name2.lower()\n\n                    # Look for death patterns mentioning either name\n                    for pattern in DEATH_PATTERNS:\n                        matches = list(re.finditer(pattern, combined_context, re.IGNORECASE))\n                        for match in matches:\n                            matched_name = match.group(1).lower()\n                            # If the death pattern mentions one of our names\n                            name1_in_match = any(part in matched_name for part in name1_lower.split() if len(part) > 2)\n                            name2_in_match = any(part in matched_name for part in name2_lower.split() if len(part) > 2)\n\n                            if name1_in_match or name2_in_match:\n                                # Check if BOTH names appear in a wider context window around the death\n                                match_pos = match.start()\n                                context_window = combined_context[max(0, match_pos-300):match_pos+300].lower()\n\n                                # More flexible matching: check if key parts of names appear\n                                name1_parts = [p for p in name1_lower.split() if len(p) > 2]\n                                name2_parts = [p for p in name2_lower.split() if len(p) > 2]\n\n                                name1_found = any(part in context_window for part in name1_parts) if name1_parts else name1_lower in context_window\n                                name2_found = any(part in context_window for part in name2_parts) if name2_parts else name2_lower in context_window\n\n                                if name1_found and name2_found:\n                                    death_evidence.append((name1, name2, context_window[:200]))  # Store first 200 chars for logging\n                                    logger.info(\n                                        f\"  Death evidence found: '{name1}' and '{name2}' both appear near death pattern\"\n                                    )"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":323,"cache_read_input_tokens":68514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":323,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"076185ae-b8e4-4f9d-b6d1-b2359811f632","uuid":"6c8482ee-e4a6-4d6a-9da8-2743099c461d"}
